// Dates, clock values and the passage of time: the `date` or `time` a value
// falls on, the `duration` between two of them, and the `timer` that fires
// every duration.
//
// None of this is ambient. A program that never asks what time it is never
// names any of it, which is why these are imported rather than in scope
// everywhere.
//
// `date`, `time` and `datetime` are string-representable, as `color` is: a
// string literal in the canonical form coerces to one, and one coerces back
// to that form. Platform codegen maps all three to the host's native
// date/time type (Go `time.Time`, JS/Kotlin string).
